research_llm: ollama local model ornith-1.5:35b

task.question_source_fine_tuning.doctors (completed) {
  - if <topic> is about a specific Dr, do the following:
    hospital: find the doctor's hospital
    titles: get all related articles's titles by searching <the doctor's name> in <hospital>
    articles: baed on the {titles}, try to pick the articles that with the title containing <the doctor's name>
    add {articles} to the context and answer the question
}

task.question_source_fine_tuning (completed) {
  - if a <topic> is about general facts, for example:
    - what is donald trump's birthday?
    - what does nvidia do?
    restrict the news search to en.wikipedia.org, get the wikipedia article and add to the context

}

task (completed) {
  when RESEARCH_WITH_NEWS_MODE is off, the previous accumulated context should be cleared
}

task.keep_track_of_previous_context (completed) {
  when RESEARCH_WITH_NEWS_MODE is on:
  for each {question} all subsequent questions {
    - each relevant question for {question} that we are going to search using "/news search" should be related to the current accumulated context
  }
}

task (completed) {
  create command /research_with_the_news <topic> {
    - starting RESEARCH_WITH_NEWS_MODE, and it will be set to be "on"
    when RESEARCH_WITH_NEWS_MODE is on {
      - clear all existing context, starting a clean context
      logic.fetch_news_and_produce_answer {
        - related_questions: use {research_llm} to come up with 2 most relevant questions regarding the topic, thse questions should not have any time/year information, we need to hyper focus on the <topic>
        - learn from /news search <keywords>, we are going to use /news search {related_questions}, for each question, get the top 3 news and put them into context
        - based on context: tell me about the <topic> in 100-250 words 
      }
      - there might be subsequent follow-up questions, for each question, treat it as a single <topic> and repeat logic.fetch_news_and_produce_answer
    }

    - to turn off RESEARCH_WITH_NEWS_MODE, we can do: /research_with_the_news off
    when RESEARCH_WITH_NEWS_MODE is off, we are back to normal chat process
  }
}
